 "finding": "Output-site selection is a platform-dependent tie for 17 of 104 cells",
 "cause": "_register_cell picks the CV whose midpoint is nearest the source soma point with key (abs(mid-x), i). Boundary-aligned CVs put the soma sample exactly on a CV boundary, so the two adjacent CV midpoints are equidistant and the choice is decided by last-bit rounding of the branch fractions (max interval discrepancy Vast vs Windows 1.31e-12), not by the rule.",
 "consequence": "Neither choice is physically wrong (adjacent CVs, both bounded by the soma sample, at most 10 um apart). It does mean the Windows construction reference cannot be reused byte-for-byte for Vast runs; the Vast build (bench-104-ei-1ms-build.json, build gate passed) is the reference for every Vast run and records the actual sites. Same cell IDs, donors, per-cell compartment counts (808,495) and contacts on both platforms.",
 "follow_up": "Deterministic tie-break with a tolerance in _register_cell, with a co-located test that reproduces an exact-tie source point; a rebuilt reference after that change re-pins sites for these 17 cells.",
